Mercury Browser: licensing
==========================

Mercury Browser is source-available. You can read, use, change, fork and share it for any
non-commercial purpose. Commercial use of the parts written for Mercury needs a separate licence
from the copyright holder.

Different files are under different licences. Each file says which one applies, in an
SPDX-License-Identifier header at its top or, for files that cannot hold a comment, in REUSE.toml.

1. PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.md)

   Files written for Mercury Browser by Mrinal Joshi and the Mercury Browser contributors
   (SPDX-License-Identifier: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0). In short: personal use, study, research,
   hobby projects and use by charities, schools, public research and government bodies are allowed,
   including changing the code and sharing your changes for those purposes. Using them in or for a
   commercial product or service, or to make money, requires a commercial licence: open an issue at
   https://github.com/thepigdestroyer/mercury-browser or contact the repository owner.

   Required Notice: Copyright © 2026 Mrinal Joshi (https://github.com/thepigdestroyer/mercury-browser)

2. Mozilla Public License 2.0 (LICENSES/MPL-2.0.txt)

   Files that came from Hermes Browser (https://github.com/KaykCaputo/hermes-browser, Copyright ©
   2026 Kayk Caputo) or contain code from it, files adapted from other projects, and Mercury's
   changes to those files (SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0). The MPL-2.0 applies to each of these
   files as a whole, whoever wrote which line.

3. Third-party code and data

   Vendored code under third_party/ and bundled data such as the filter lists keep their own
   licences; see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md and the other files in LICENSES/.

Versions of Mercury Browser published before this licence change (17 November 2026) were released
entirely under the MPL-2.0 and remain available under it.

This summary is for convenience; the licence texts in LICENSES/ are what apply. See NOTICE for the
copyright notice.
